(* Probe P5, first half: the ideal execution of PGL(2,7) at every prior       *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* The eight-card orbit instance has two probability models over one          *)
(* execution: the exact shuffle, which draws its cut uniformly from PGL(2,7), *)
(* and the two-hundred-letter word walk, which draws it by evaluating a       *)
(* sampled generator word. The word model is indexed by the law of the dealt  *)
(* secret and the exact model of pgl27_models.v is not: its family index is   *)
(* the unit type and its one member fixes the uniform secret. A proximity     *)
(* certificate compares the two models at one index, so an ideal indexed by   *)
(* unit can only be the ideal of a word model at the uniform prior, and the   *)
(* distance of the word model at another prior to that one ideal is the       *)
(* distance between the two priors, which is not small. The family below is   *)
(* the exact shuffle carrying the prior as its index, so that the ideal and   *)
(* the actual model speak of one secret law at every index.                   *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* Its privacy is exact at every prior and not only at the uniform one:       *)
(* pgl27_view_indep_gen is three-transitivity of PGL(2,7) on the eight points *)
(* read as a privacy statement, and three-transitivity says nothing about how *)
(* the secret is drawn. That is why the ideal this file publishes is an       *)
(* execution whose coalitions below four seats learn nothing at all, and not  *)
(* merely a law the word model happens to be near.                            *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* Definitions:                                                               *)
(*   pgl27_prior_sample        == the exact-shuffle sample layer at a prior   *)
(*   pgl27_prior_exact_family  == that layer as a prior-indexed family        *)
(*   pgl27_prior_exact_witness == its exact-arm witness                       *)
(*   pgl27_row_prior_exact_tableau                                            *)
(*                             == the ideal published as its own program      *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* Key results:                                                               *)
(*   pgl27_prior_viewE         == the framework's reading of a coalition is   *)
(*                                the instance's coalition view               *)
(*   pgl27_row_prior_exact_armE                                               *)
(*                             == the ideal row carries the exact arm         *)
(*   pgl27_row_prior_exact_rowE                                               *)
(*                             == the manifest row the ideal program          *)
(*                                publishes, in full                          *)
(******************************************************************************)

